<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Democratic Party (Uganda)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1954</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Democratic Party is a Ugandan political party founded in 1954, which drew much of its support from Catholics, particularly in Buganda. Its leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benedicto-kiwanuka">Benedicto Kiwanuka</a> headed the government under internal self-government in 1961–1962, but it lost the pre-independence election of 1962 to the alliance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uganda-peoples-congress">Uganda People's Congress</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabaka-yekka">Kabaka Yekka</a>. It was the main opposition party in the disputed election of 1980.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/democratic-party-uganda.jpg" alt="Democratic Party (Uganda)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Democratic Party · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Democratic_Party_of_Uganda.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
